---
description: Plan HyperFrames films in this Cursor chat, then render with BAML
alwaysApply: true
---

When asked for a video, write one `FilmPlan` story that matches `baml_src/film.baml` and run `baml run main -- --plan_file videos/<slug>/plan.json`. That writes one `plan.json`. `voice_id` and `avatar_id` stay empty until the Studio reviews below. Follow this order and stop at each review.

Studio lists composition files by filename, in alphabetical order. Keep the beats in the same order as the Notion `Scene_id` column, starting at 1. The publisher zero-pads that number to the width of the scene count, then names each file `compositions/<Scene_id>-<id>.html`. A ten-scene film uses `01` through `10`. A hundred-scene film uses `001` through `100`. A four-scene film stays `1-hello` before `2-pipeline`. Leave the beat id as a word. A CSS selector cannot start with a digit.

The card is the Hyperframes Genie row whose `Slug` is the video folder. Each command below sets `Status` to one of these options. `Preview cut`, `Studio review`, `HeyGen voice`, `Voice review`, `Lip-sync avatar`, `Done`, `Rework`. With `NOTION_TOKEN` or `NOTION_API_KEY` set, the command writes that option. Set the same option on the card before you stop.

1. Preview cut, silent: still avatar and no voice. `baml run render_cut -- --dir videos/<slug> --cut preview` writes `renders/preview-cut.mp4` and opens HyperFrames Studio. Give the person the `studioUrl`. `Status` becomes `Studio review`. `Lastest Studio Link` becomes that URL. `Silent Preview Cut (mp4)` becomes `videos/<slug>/renders/preview-cut.mp4`.
2. Wait for their review. Then `baml run approve -- --dir videos/<slug> --stage preview`, or `reject` if they say no. Approval sets `Status` to `HeyGen voice`. A rejection sets `Status` to `Rework`.
3. Add the HeyGen voice: `baml run swap_voice -- --dir videos/<slug> --voice_id <heygen-voice>`. The avatar stays a still. The preview had no voice. The `voice_id` is often not an avatar's default voice. This does not call HeyGen. `Voice_id` is saved on the card. `Status` stays `HeyGen voice`.
4. Open Studio again: `baml run open_studio -- --dir videos/<slug> --cut voice`. That sets `Status` to `Voice review` and refreshes `Lastest Studio Link`. Wait for that review, then `baml run approve -- --dir videos/<slug> --stage voice`. Approval sets `Status` to `Lip-sync avatar`. A rejection sets `Status` to `Rework`.
5. Add the HeyGen lip-sync avatar only after that voice review: `baml run add_lipsync -- --dir videos/<slug> --avatar_id <avatar>`. It keeps the reviewed `voice_id`. `Avatar_id` is saved on the card. `Status` becomes `Done`. Do not start the paid lip-sync, do not call HeyGen, and do not ask for an API key.

Republishing the story deletes `reviews.json` and sets `Status` back to `Preview cut`. The subscription model in this chat is the planner.
